/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-------------------------------*\
  envelope01_natural_gas -- the P-T phase envelope of a lean natural gas.

  WHAT IT DEMONSTRATES, and the second half is the point:

    * the DEW branch traced in pressure, over the cricondentherm -- marching
      P, the temperature maximum is not a turning point for the
      specification, so the trace walks straight over it and the maximum is
      visible in the data;

    * the BUBBLE branch producing NOTHING, announced as what it is.  This
      feed is 80 % methane and its bubble line lies below the saturation
      solver's own 200 K bracket.  A branch that never started is NOT a
      branch that stopped at a turning point, and the two are reported
      differently because the remedies differ.

  NOT CLAIMED: the nose.  A pressure-marched trace cannot pass the
  cricondenbar, nor the critical point where the branches merge.  Closing it
  needs arc-length continuation with a switching specification (Michelsen,
  Fluid Phase Equilib. 4 (1980) 1) and that is not implemented.

  NOT VALIDATED: no number here is checked against a measured envelope.  The
  feed is a plausible lean gas, not a sampled one, and the K-values come from
  Peng-Robinson over an ideal liquid.  This is a STRUCTURAL witness -- it
  shows what the op reports and refuses to report, not that the curve is
  right.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoProps;
description   "P-T phase envelope of a lean natural gas: the dew branch over its cricondentherm, and a bubble branch that never starts";
verbosity     3;
